Have you looked at dfns (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Direct_function)? They allow you something very similar. Compare Dijkstra's GCL:
  if a < b → c := true    □ a ≥ b → c := false   fi  To an APL dfn with "guards":
  c ← {         a < b : true         a ≥ b : false       }  As in GCL, if none of the guards hold true, the dfn (braces) will terminate without return value, and thus the code will abort with an error.
